# Benchmark box (NVIDIA). One pinned file cannot span Apple Silicon and CUDA, so the
# published numbers are produced from this one and it names the torch build exactly.
#
# NOTE: `make lock-gpu` only runs on Linux — triton publishes no macOS wheels, so this
# file cannot be compiled on the dev Mac. Generate requirements-gpu.txt on the rented
# box (Day 12) and commit it from there; that is also the machine whose numbers get
# published, so the lockfile and the results come from the same environment.
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu124

-r requirements.in
triton          # S3 (stretch, Day 14) — pinned here so the GPU env is reproducible either way
